<!--
=============================================================================

 FUNC_* ENTITIES

=============================================================================
-->

  <group name="func_group" color="0 .5 .8">
Editor utility for grouping world brushes and patches. The entity never reaches the game: its geometry is merged into worldspawn with per-surface overrides taken from this entity's keys.
-------- KEYS --------
<real key="smooth" name="Lightmap Smooth Radius">Lightmap smoothing radius for the group's surfaces (0 disables).</real>
<color key="vertexcolor" name="Vertex Color">Override the vertex color.</color>
<real key="vertexalpha" name="Vertex Alpha">Override opacity (0..1 or 0..255).</real>
<boolean key="upscale" name="Upscale Raytracing">Raytrace these surfaces at 2x lightmap resolution.</boolean>
<real key="supersample" name="Supersample Radius">Supersampling trace radius (0 = off).</real>
<real key="samplesize" name="Lightmap Sample Size">Lightmap sample size override. Alias: lightmapsamplesize.</real>
<boolean key="enforcesamplesize" name="Enforce Sample Size">Subdivide to honour the sample size.</boolean>
<boolean key="castshadows" name="Cast Shadows">Cast shadows into the lightmap (default 1). Alias: cs.</boolean>
<string key="modelgroup" name="Model Group">Bind misc_model entities with the same modelgroup.</string>
<string key="decalgroup" name="Decal Group">Only decals with a matching decalgroup project here.</string>
<real key="chamfer_convexwidth" name="Convex Chamfer Width">Per-entity convex-edge chamfer width.</real>
<real key="chamfer_concavewidth" name="Concave Chamfer Width">Per-entity concave-edge chamfer width.</real>
<boolean key="nosolid" name="Render Only">Render geometry without collision. Also nonsolid / collisiontype none.</boolean>
-------- TERRAIN MODE (legacy) --------
<boolean key="terrain" name="Terrain Mode">Set to 1 to treat this group as terrain.</boolean>
<texture key="shader" name="Terrain MetaShader">Metashader used to assign terrain textures.</texture>
<texture key="alphamap" name="Terrain Blending Map">Art file guiding texture blending on the terrain.</texture>
<integer key="layers" name="Terrain Layers">Number of unique root shaders used by the terrain.</integer>
-------- NOTES --------
Use TAB to cycle through the component pieces of a selected func_group. For a dedicated terrain generator, use func_terrain instead.
collisiontype none (also nonsolid) is accepted by the compiler for render-only brushes; it has no editor widget.
  </group>

  <group name="func_bobbing" color="0 .5 .8">
Solid entity that oscillates back and forth in a linear motion. Entity bobs on the Z axis (up-down) by default. It can also emit sound if the "noise" key is set. Will crush the player when blocked. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<real key="speed" name="Speed">amount of time in seconds for one complete oscillation cycle (default 4).</real>
<real key="height" name="Height">sets the amount of travel of the oscillation movement (default 32).</real>
<real key="phase" name="Phase">sets the start offset of the oscillation cycle. Values must be 0 &lt; phase &lt; 1. Any integer phase value is the same as no offset (default 0).</real>
<sound key="noise_start" name="Start Sound">start moving sound (default is silent)</sound>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">path/name of .wav file to play (default is silent). Use looping sounds only (eg. sound/world/drone6.wav - See Notes).</sound>
<sound key="noise_stop" name="Stop Sound">stop moving sound (default is silent)</sound>
<model key="model2" name="Model File">path/name of model to include.</model>
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">alternate method of setting XYZ origin of sound and .md3 model included with entity (See Notes).</real3>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">constantLight radius of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 0).</real>
<color key="_color" name="Color">constantLight color of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 1 1 1).</color>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="X_AXIS" name="X Axis" bit="0">Use/rotate around the X axis.</flag>
<flag key="Y_AXIS" name="Y Axis" bit="1">Use/rotate around the Y axis.</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
In order for the sound to be emitted from the entity, it is recommended to include a brush with an origin shader at its center, otherwise the sound will not follow the entity as it moves. Setting the origin key is simply an alternate method to using an origin brush. When using the model2 key, the origin point of the model will correspond to the origin point defined by either the origin brush or the origin coordinate value.
Start and stop sounds will only be played if the entity is set to be triggered
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_button" color="0 .5 .8">
When a button is touched by a player, it moves in the direction set by the "angle" key, triggers all its targets, stays pressed by an amount of time set by the "wait" key, then returns to it's original position where it can be operated again. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<direction key="angle" name="Direction">determines the direction in which the button will move (up = -1, down = -2).</direction>
<target key="target" name="Target">all entities with a matching targetname will be triggered.</target>
<real key="speed" name="Speed">speed of button's displacement (default 40).</real>
<real key="wait" name="Delay">Number of seconds the button stays pressed (default 3, -1 = return immediately).</real>
<real key="lip" name="Lip">lip remaining at end of move (default 4 units).</real>
<real key="health" name="Health">(default 0) if set to any non-zero value, the button must take damage (any amount) to activate.</real>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">custom noise to be played when activated</sound>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">constantLight radius of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 0).</real>
<color key="_color" name="Color">constantLight color of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 1 1 1).</color>
<model key="model2" name="Model File">path/name of model to include (eg: models/mapobjects/pipe/pipe02.md3).</model>
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">alternate method of setting XYZ origin of .md3 model included with entity (See Notes).</real3>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- NOTES --------
Setting the origin key is simply an alternate method to using an origin brush. When using the model2 key, the origin point of the model will correspond to the origin point defined by either the origin brush or the origin coordinate value.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_door" color="0 .5 .8">
Normal sliding door entity. By default, the door will activate when player walks close to it or when damage is inflicted to it. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<string key="message" name="Message">is printed when the door is touched if it is a trigger door and it hasn't been fired yet</string>
<direction key="angle" name="Direction">determines the opening direction of door (up = -1, down = -2).</direction>
<real key="speed" name="Speed">determines how fast the door moves (default 600).</real>
<real key="wait" name="Delay">number of seconds before door returns (2 default, -1 = never return)</real>
<real key="lip" name="Lip">lip remaining at end of move (default 8)</real>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">if set, a func_button or trigger is required to activate the door.</targetname>
<target key="target" name="Target">fire entities with this targetname when activated</target>
<real key="health" name="Health">(default 0) if set to any non-zero value, the button must take damage (any amount) to activate.</real>
<integer key="dmg" name="Damage">damage to inflict on player when he blocks operation of door (default 2). Door will reverse direction when blocked unless CRUSHER spawnflag is set.</integer>
<string key="team" name="Team Name">assign the same team name to multiple doors that should operate together (see Notes).</string>
<integer key="gameteam" name="Team Filter">makes the door only openable by a player of a specific team (0 = everyone, 1 = FFA players, 2 = alpha,  3 = beta)</integer>
<sound key="noise_start" name="Start Sound">overrides default start moving sound</sound>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">overrides default movement sound</sound>
<sound key="noise_stop" name="Stop Sound">overrides default stop moving sound</sound>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">constantLight radius of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 0).</real>
<color key="_color" name="Color">constantLight color of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 1 1 1).</color>
<model key="model2" name="Model File">path/name of model to include (eg: models/mapobjects/pipe/pipe02.md3).</model>
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">alternate method of setting XYZ origin of .md3 model included with entity (See Notes).</real3>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="START_OPEN" name="Start Open" bit="0">the door will spawn in the open state and operate in reverse.</flag>
<flag key="CRUSHER" name="Crusher" bit="2">door will not reverse direction when blocked and will keep damaging player until he dies or gets out of the way.</flag>
<flag key="NOMONSTER" name="Nomonster" bit="3">monsters will not trigger this door</flag>
<flag key="TOGGLE" name="Toggle" bit="5">wait in both the start and end states for a trigger event</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_pendulum" color="0 .5 .8">
You need to have an origin brush as part of this entity. Solid entity that describes a pendulum back and forth rotation movement. Rotates on the X axis by default. Pendulum frequency is a physical constant based on the length of the beam and gravity. Blocking the pendulum instantly kills a player. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle">angle offset of axis of rotation from default X axis (default 0).</angle>
<real key="speed" name="Speed">angle of swing arc in either direction from initial position (default 30).</real>
<real key="phase" name="Phase">sets the start offset of the swinging cycle. Values must be 0 &lt; phase &lt; 1. Any integer phase value is the same as no offset (default 0).</real>
<sound key="noise_start" name="Start Sound">start moving sound to be played only if triggered (default is silent)</sound>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">path/name of .wav file to play. Use looping sounds only (default is silent).</sound>
<sound key="noise_stop" name="Stop Sound">stop moving sound to be played only if triggered (default is silent)</sound>
<model key="model2" name="Model File">path/name of model to include (eg: models/mapobjects/jets/jets01.md3).</model>
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">alternate method of setting XYZ origin of entity's rotation axis and .md3 model included with entity (default "0 0 0" - See Notes).</real3>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">constantLight radius of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 0).</real>
<color key="_color" name="Color">constantLight color of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 1 1 1).</color>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- NOTES --------
You need to have an origin brush as part of this entity. The center of that brush will be the point through which the rotation axis passes. Setting the origin key is simply an alternate method to using an origin brush. Pendulum will rotate along the X axis by default. Very crude operation: pendulum cannot rotate along Z axis, the speed of swing (frequency) is not adjustable. When using the model2 key, the origin point of the model will correspond to the origin point defined by either the origin brush or the origin coordinate value. Pendulums always swing north / south on unrotated models. Add an angles field to the model to allow rotation in other directions. Pendulum frequency is a physical constant based on the length of the beam and gravity.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_plat" color="0 .5 .8">
Rising platform the player can ride to reach higher places. Plats must always be drawn in the raised position, so they will operate and be lighted correctly but they spawn in the lowered position. The plat will stay in the raised position until the player steps off. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<real key="speed" name="Speed">How fast the platform moves (default 300).</real>
<real key="accel" name="Accel">default 20</real>
<real key="deccel" name="Deccel">default 20</real>
<real key="lip" name="Lip">Lip remaining at the end of the move (default 8).</real>
<real key="height" name="Height">if set, this will determine the total amount of vertical travel of the plat, instead of being implicitly assigned by the model's height.</real>
<integer key="dmg" name="Damage">Damage inflicted when the platform blocks the player (default 2).</integer>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">if set, the trigger that points to this will raise the plat each time it fires.</targetname>
<sound key="noise_start" name="Start Sound">overrides default start moving sound</sound>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">overrides default movement sound</sound>
<sound key="noise_stop" name="Stop Sound">overrides default stop moving sound</sound>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">constantLight radius of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 0).</real>
<color key="_color" name="Color">constantLight color of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 1 1 1).</color>
<model key="model2" name="Model File">path/name of model to include (eg: models/mapobjects/pipe/pipe02.md3).</model>
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">alternate method of setting XYZ origin of .md3 model included with entity (See Notes).</real3>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="LOW_TRIGGER" name="Low Trigger" bit="0">the plat is triggered from its lower side</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
By default, the total amount of vertical travel of a platform is implicitly determined by the overall vertical size of the brushes of which it's made minus the lip value. But if the "height" key is used, then the total amount of vertical travel of the plat will be exactly that value regardless of the shape and size of the plat and regardless of the value of the "lip" key. Using the "height" key is the best method for any kind of platforms and the only possible one for thin plats which need to travel vertical distances many times their own thickness. Setting the origin key is simply an alternate method to using an origin brush. When using the model2 key, the origin point of the model will correspond to the origin point defined by either the origin brush or the origin coordinate value.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_rotating" color="0 .5 .8">
You need to have an origin brush as part of this entity.  The center of that brush will be
the point around which it is rotated. It will rotate around the Z axis by default.  You can
check either the X_AXIS or Y_AXIS box to change that. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">name to be targeted</targetname>
<target key="target" name="Target">names to target.</target>
<real key="speed" name="Speed">determines how fast entity rotates (default 100).</real>
<sound key="noise_start" name="Start Sound">overrides default start moving sound</sound>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">overrides default movement sound</sound>
<sound key="noise_stop" name="Stop Sound">overrides default stop moving sound</sound>
<model key="model2" name="Model File">path/name of model to include (eg: models/mapobjects/bitch/fembotbig.md3).</model>
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">alternate method of setting XYZ origin of entity's rotation axis and .md3 model included with entity (default "0 0 0" - See Notes).</real3>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">constantLight radius of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 0).</real>
<color key="_color" name="Color">constantLight color of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 1 1 1).</color>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="START_OFF" name="Start Off" bit="0">Start in the off state.</flag>
<flag key="REVERSE" name="Reverse" bit="1">Reverse the normal direction of travel.</flag>
<flag key="X_AXIS" name="X Axis" bit="2">Use/rotate around the X axis.</flag>
<flag key="Y_AXIS" name="Y Axis" bit="3">Use/rotate around the Y axis.</flag>
<flag key="TOUCH_PAIN" name="Touch Pain" bit="4">Damage players on contact.</flag>
<flag key="STOP" name="Stop" bit="5">Stop rotating when touched.</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
You need to have an origin brush as part of this entity. The center of that brush will be the point through which the rotation axis passes. Setting the origin key is simply an alternate method to using an origin brush. It will rotate along the Z axis by default. You can check either the X_AXIS or Y_AXIS box to change that. When using the model2 key, the origin point of the model will correspond to the origin point defined by either the origin brush or the origin coordinate value.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_train" color="0 .5 .8">
Trains are moving platforms that players can ride. The targets origin specifies the min point of the train at each corner. The train spawns at the first target it is pointing at. If the train is the target of a button or trigger, it will not begin moving until activated. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<real key="speed" name="Speed">speed of displacement of train (default 100).</real>
<integer key="dmg" name="Damage">default 2</integer>
<target key="target" name="Target">point to first entity in the path</target>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">train's targetname</targetname>
<sound key="noise_start" name="Start Sound">start moving sound (default silent)</sound>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">movement sound (default silent)</sound>
<sound key="noise_stop" name="Stop Sound">stop moving sound (default silent)</sound>
<model key="model2" name="Model File">path/name of model to include (eg: models/mapobjects/pipe/pipe02.md3).</model>
