  <group name="func_wall" color="0 .5 .8">
This is just a solid wall if not inhibited. Can be used for conditional walls. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<target key="target" name="Target">activate entities with this targetname when used</target>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">use this name to target me</targetname>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="TRIGGER_SPAWN" name="Trigger Spawn" bit="0">the wall will not be present until triggered it will then blink in to existance; it will kill anything that was in its way</flag>
<flag key="TOGGLE" name="Toggle" bit="1">only valid for TRIGGER_SPAWN walls this allows the wall to be turned on and off</flag>
<flag key="START_ON" name="Start On" bit="2">only valid for TRIGGER_SPAWN walls the wall will initially be present</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
Untested in Warfork
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_static" color="0 .5 .8">
Static non-solid bspmodel. Can be used for conditional walls and models. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<model key="model2" name="Model File">path/name of model to include (eg: models/mapobjects/bitch/fembotbig.md3).</model>
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">alternate method of setting XYZ origin of .md3 model included with entity (See Notes).</real3>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">constantLight radius of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 0).</real>
<color key="_color" name="Color">constantLight color of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 1 1 1).</color>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">NOT SUPPORTED BY RENDERER - if set, a func_button or trigger can make entity disappear from the game (See Notes).</targetname>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- NOTES --------
When using the model2 key, the origin point of the model will correspond to the origin point defined by either the origin brush or the origin coordinate value. If a model is included with a targeted func_static, the brush(es) of the entity will be removed from the game but the .md3 model won't: it will automatically be moved to the (0 0 0) world origin so you should NOT include an .md3 model to a targeted func_static.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_object" color="0 .5 .8">
This is solid bmodel that will fall if its support it removed. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">alternate method of setting XYZ origin of .md3 model included with entity (See Notes).</real3>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">constantLight radius of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 0).</real>
<color key="_color" name="Color">constantLight color of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 1 1 1).</color>
<target key="target" name="Target">fire targets with this name at being used.</target>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">name to be targeted with.</targetname>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="TRIGGER_SPAWN" name="Trigger Spawn" bit="0">spawn this entity when target is fired</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
model2 is not supported in func_objects, only map brushes can be safely used as model
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_explosive" color="0 .5 .8">
Any brush that you want to explode or break apart.If you want an
explosion, set dmg and it will do a radius explosion of that amount
at the center of the bursh. If targeted it will not be shootable. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<real key="health" name="Health">defaults to 100.</real>
<real key="mass" name="Mass">defaults to 75.  This determines how much debris is emitted when it explodes.  You get one large chunk per 100 of mass (up to 8) and one small chunk per 25 of mass (up to 16).  So 800 gives the most.</real>
<model key="model2" name="Model File">a md3 model.</model>
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">alternate method of setting XYZ origin of .md3 model included with entity (See Notes).</real3>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">constantLight radius of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 0).</real>
<color key="_color" name="Color">constantLight color of .md3 model included with entity. Has no effect on the entity's brushes (default 1 1 1).</color>
<target key="target" name="Target">fire targets with this name at being used.</target>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">name to be targeted with.</targetname>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="TRIGGER_SPAWN" name="Trigger Spawn" bit="0">spawn this entity when target is fired</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
Untested: model2 models might not collide perfectly if used with a brush origin
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="func_clock" color="0 0 1" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Target a target_string with this, to print a clock. The default is to be a time of day clock (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<target key="target" name="Target">fire targets with this name at being used.</target>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">name to be targeted with.</targetname>
<target key="pathtarget" name="Path Target">countdown will fire this one</target>
<integer key="count" name="Count">a value.</integer>
<integer key="style" name="Style">0 "xx", 1 "xx:xx", 2 "xx:xx:xx"</integer>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="TIMER_UP" name="Timer Up" bit="0">run for "count" seconds and then fire target.</flag>
<flag key="TIMER_DOWN" name="Timer Down" bit="1">run for "count" seconds and then fire target.</flag>
<flag key="START_OFF" name="Start Off" bit="2">Start in the off state.</flag>
<flag key="MULTI_USE" name="Multi Use" bit="3">can be used more than once.</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
Untested
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="_decal" color="0 .5 .8">
This is not an entity as such, it never reaches the game. It is strictly an editor utility to project decal surfaces onto map geometry (brushes, patches and misc_model surfaces).
-------- KEYS --------
<target key="target" name="Target">Optional point entity that sets the projection direction and bounds. If omitted, makebsp projects along the calculated surface normal (or straight down).</target>
<real key="distance" name="Projection Depth">Projection depth (default 64). Alias: depth.</real>
<string key="decalgroup" name="Decal Group">Only project onto receivers with a matching decalgroup.</string>
<real key="patchSubdivision" name="Patch Subdivision">Receiver-patch tessellation resolution (default 0.4, min 0.05).</real>
<color key="vertexcolor" name="Vertex Color">Decal vertex color override. Alias: _color.</color>
<real key="vertexalpha" name="Vertex Alpha">Decal opacity override.</real>
-------- NOTES --------
In makebsp the _decal entity can contain one or more brush solids and/or curved Bezier patches as its projection source - a patch mesh is not required, and brushes and patches can be mixed freely in the same entity. The target key is optional; without it the projection direction is derived from the surface normal (or straight down). (q3map2 requires a patch mesh and a target.) Distance alphablending is not supported.
  </group>


