  </point>

  <group name="trigger_push" color=".5 .5 .5">
This is used to create jump pads and launch ramps. It MUST point to a target_position or info_notnull entity to work. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<target key="target" name="Target">this points to the target_position to which the player will jump.</target>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">override default noise ("silent" doesn't make any noise)</sound>
<real key="wait" name="Delay">time before it can be triggered again.</real>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="PUSH_ONCE" name="Push Once" bit="0">only push when touched the first time</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
To make a jump pad or launch ramp, place the target_position/info_notnull entity at the highest point of the jump and target it with this entity.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="trigger_multiple" color=".5 .5 .5">
Variable size repeatable trigger. It will fire the entities it targets when touched by player. Can be made to operate like a trigger_once entity by setting the "wait" key to -1. It can also be activated by another trigger that targets it. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<target key="target" name="Target">this points to the entity to activate.</target>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">activating trigger points to this.</targetname>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">play this noise when triggered</sound>
<string key="message" name="Message">centerprint this text string when triggered</string>
<real key="wait" name="Delay">time in seconds until trigger becomes re-triggerable after it's been touched (default 0.2, -1 = trigger once).</real>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="MONSTER" name="Monster" bit="0">monsters won't activate this trigger unless this flag is set</flag>
<flag key="NOT_PLAYER" name="Not Player" bit="1">players can't trigger this one (for those triggered by other triggers)</flag>
<flag key="TRIGGERED" name="Triggered" bit="2">spawns as triggered and must wait for the "wait" key to pass to be re-triggered</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
message is untested
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </group>

  <group name="trigger_once" color=".5 .5 .5">
Triggers once, then removes itself. You must set the key "target" to the name of another object in the level that has a matching "targetname". (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
