  <point name="misc_teleporter_dest" color="1 .5 .25" box="-32 -32 -24 32 32 -16">
Teleport destination location point for trigger_teleporter entities. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle">direction in which player will look when teleported.</angle>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">make the trigger_teleporter point to this.</targetname>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- NOTES --------
Does the same thing as info_teleport_destination
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </point>

  <point name="misc_model" color="1 .5 .25" box="-16 -16 -16 16 16 16">
Compiler-only model instance: makebsp bakes the model into the BSP at compile time. Supported formats: md3, iqm, md5mesh, obj, 3ds, ase, fbx, gltf, glb, lwo.
-------- KEYS --------
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">Base translation/position of the model (X Y Z).</real3>
<angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle">Yaw angle, used only when angles is 0 0 0.</angle>
<angles key="angles" name="Pitch Yaw Roll">Model orientation in PITCH YAW ROLL.</angles>
<model key="model" name="Model File">Path to the model file to load.</model>
<string key="modelscale" name="Model Scale">Uniform scale factor applied to all axes (default 1).</string>
<real3 key="modelscale_vec" name="Non-uniform Scale">Non-uniform scale vector (X Y Z); 0 0 0 falls back to modelscale. A negative determinant flips the winding.</real3>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">Name matched by a func_trim entity's target key, limiting trimming to this model.</targetname>
<real key="smooth" name="Lightmap Smooth Radius">Lightmap smoothing radius for the model (0 disables).</real>
<string key="smoothgroup" name="Smooth Group">Shared smoothing group for kitbashed models.</string>
<color key="vertexcolor" name="Vertex Color">Override the vertex color.</color>
<real key="vertexalpha" name="Vertex Alpha">Override opacity (0..1 or 0..255).</real>
<boolean key="upscale" name="Upscale Raytracing">Raytrace at 2x lightmap resolution.</boolean>
<real key="supersample" name="Supersample Radius">Supersampling trace radius (0 = off).</real>
<real key="samplesize" name="Lightmap Sample Size">Lightmap sample size override. Alias: lightmapsamplesize.</real>
<real key="lightmapscale" name="Lightmap Scale">Lightmap resolution factor (0.01..16, default 1).</real>
<boolean key="forceuvgen" name="Force Lightmap UVs">Generate fresh lightmap UVs instead of using the model's UVs.</boolean>
<boolean key="castshadows" name="Cast Shadows">Cast shadows into the lightmap (default 1). Alias: cs.</boolean>
<string key="collisiontype" name="Collision Type">object (default), wrap, extrude, objectdetail, wrapdetail, terrain, none/nosolid/nonsolid.</string>
<string key="modelgroup" name="Model Group">Bind this model to a brush entity with the same modelgroup. Alias: modelsgroup.</string>
<string key="decalgroup" name="Decal Group">Only decals with a matching decalgroup project onto this model.</string>
<integer key="maxtriangles" name="Max Triangles">Triangle budget before decimation. Alias: maxtriangle.</integer>
<real key="light" name="Light Intensity">Only for models using the tag_light shader: intensity of the generated lights.</real>
<string key="lighttype" name="Light Type">Only for tag_light models: point/pointlight generates point lights; anything else generates spotlights.</string>
-------- NOTES --------
makebsp ignores the legacy q3map2 keys _frame, _remap* (including _remap2, etc.), _castshadows, _receiveshadows and _lightmapscale, and it ignores misc_model spawnflags entirely. Use samplesize, castshadows and lightmapscale instead.
With type set to surface/surfacelight, makebsp also applies these surface-light keys to the model surfaces: light, color, backsplash, subdivide, cutoff, fadeout, nodeluxe, backsplash_nodeluxe, grid_ambientscale, grid_directscale and attenuation.
Models using the tag_light shader (shown as a triangle in the editor) emit a real light from each triangle. makebsp spawns one light entity per triangle and copies all of this entity's keys onto it (except classname, origin, model and smooth), so a tag_light model can use all the same keys as the light entity - color, light, radius, softness, attenuation, target/dir, cutoff, etc. lighttype point/pointlight makes point lights; anything else makes spotlights.
  </point>

  <point name="misc_portal_camera" color="1 .5 .25" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Portal camera. This camera is used to project its view onto a portal surface in the level through the intermediary of a misc_portal_surface entity. Use the "angles" key or target a target_position or info_notnull entity to set the camera's pointing direction. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<angles key="angles" name="Pitch Yaw Roll">this sets the pitch and yaw aiming angles of the portal camera (default 0 0). Use "roll" key to set roll angle.</angles>
<target key="target" name="Target">point this to a target_position entity to set the camera's pointing direction.</target>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">a misc_portal_surface portal surface indicator must point to this.</targetname>
<angle key="roll" name="Camera Roll">roll angle of camera. A value of 0 is upside down and 180 is the same as the player's view.</angle>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="SLOWROTATE" name="Slowrotate" bit="0">makes the portal camera rotate slowly along the roll axis.</flag>
<flag key="FASTROTATE" name="Fastrotate" bit="1">makes the portal camera rotate faster along the roll axis.</flag>
<flag key="NOROTATE" name="Norotate" bit="2">disables rotation</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
Both the setting "angles" key or "targeting a target_position" methods can be used to aim the camera. However, the target_position method is simpler. In both cases, the "roll" key must be used to set the roll angle. If either the SLOWROTATE or FASTROTATE spawnflag is set, then the "roll" value is irrelevant.
  </point>

  <point name="misc_portal_surface" color="1 .5 .25" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
The portal surface nearest this entity will show a view from the targeted misc_portal_camera, or a mirror view if untargeted. This must be within 64 world units of the surface! (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- NOTES --------
The entity must be no farther than 64 units away from the portal surface to lock onto it. To make a mirror, apply the common/mirror shader to the surface, place this entity near it but don't target a misc_portal_camera.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </point>

  <point name="misc_skyportal" color="1 .5 .25" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Camera of a portal view which will show up at the sky
-------- KEYS --------
<boolean key="noents" name="Hide Sky Entities">when set to 1 the entities in the sky room will be skept from drawing.</boolean>
<real key="fov" name="Field of View">when set to any value it will override the player fov. Do not set for normal behavior.</real>
<real key="scale" name="View Scale">scale the view to make it appear closer or further.</real>
-------- NOTES --------
The entity must be placed in a room which is not connected to the rest of the map.
  </point>

  <point name="misc_explobox" color="1 .5 .25" box="-16 -16 0 16 16 40">
-------- KEYS --------
<target key="target" name="Target">fire entities with this targetname at exploding</target>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">to explode by being triggered.</targetname>
<real key="health" name="Health">default 80</real>
<real key="mass" name="Mass">influences the ammount of debris at exploding (default 100)</real>
<integer key="dmg" name="Damage">damage radius of the explosion (default 150)</integer>
<angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle">direction in which model will be oriented.</angle>
<model key="model" name="Model File">path/name of model to use (eg: models/mapobjects/barrel/barrel.md3).</model>
  </point>

  <point name="misc_capture_area_indicator" color="1 .5 .25" box="-16 -16 0 16 16 96" model="models/objects/capture_area/indicator.md3">
Indicator of the capture area for domination alike gametypes
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="SUSPENDED" name="Suspended" bit="0">Float: disable gravity and do not drop the item to the floor.</flag>
  </point>

  <point name="misc_particles" color=".6 .7 .7" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Generates particles
-------- KEYS --------
<angles key="angles" name="Pitch Yaw Roll">direction in which the particles will be thrown (unused when spherical).</angles>
<real key="radius" name="Radius">radius of the spread of the particles direction (unused when spherical).</real>
<texture key="shaderName" name="Shader Name">the particle shader to use.</texture>
<real key="size" name="Particle Size">the radius of a particle.</real>
<real key="delay" name="Fade Delay">time before the particle dissapears.</real>
<integer key="gameteam" name="Team Filter">use teamcolors on the sprites. 2 ALPHA, 3 BETA.</integer>
<real key="speed" name="Speed">Speed at which the particles will be thrown</real>
<integer key="count" name="Count">Number of particles per second</integer>
<color key="_color" name="Color">color of the light emitted by the particle.</color>
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">the entity (not each particle) produces this looping sound.</sound>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="SPHERICAL" name="Spherical" bit="0">Particles will be generated in all directions around a point</flag>
<flag key="SOLID" name="Solid" bit="1">Particles will bounce on walls</flag>
<flag key="GRAVITY" name="Gravity" bit="2">Particles will be affected by gravity</flag>
<flag key="LIGHT" name="Light" bit="3">enable light on the particles</flag>
<flag key="EXPAND_EFFECT" name="Expand Effect" bit="4">The particle expands during its lifetime</flag>
<flag key="SHRINK_EFFECT" name="Shrink Effect" bit="5">The particle shrinks during its lifetime</flag>
<flag key="START_OFF" name="Start Off" bit="6">Start in the off state.</flag>
  </point>


