=============================================================================

 TARGET_* ENTITIES

=============================================================================
-->

  <point name="target_give" color="0 .5 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
This is used to give ammo, weapons, health or items to the player who activates it.
-------- KEYS --------
<target key="target" name="Target">this points to the item(s) to give when activated.</target>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">activating trigger or spawn entity points to this.</targetname>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- NOTES --------
There are 2 ways to use this entity.
a) automatically give items to players when they spawn in the game: make a spawn location entity like info_player_deathmatch or CTF respawn points target this entity, then make it target the item(s) to give to the player upon respawn.
b) give items to players during the game: make a trigger_multiple target this entity, then make it target the item(s) to give to the player when the trigger is touched.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </point>

  <point name="target_startTimer" color="1 0 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Timer Start
  </point>

  <point name="target_stopTimer" color="1 0 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Timer Stop
-------- KEYS --------
<target key="target" name="Target">stopTimer triggers its targets when a best time occurs.</target>
  </point>

  <point name="target_checkpoint" color="1 0 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Checkpoint
  </point>

  <point name="target_location" color="0 .5 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Location marker used by bots and players for team orders and team chat in the course of Teamplay games. The closest target_location in sight is used for the location. If none is in sight, the closest in distance is used. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<string key="message" name="Message">name of the location (text string). Displayed in parentheses in front of all team chat and order messages.</string>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- NOTES --------
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </point>

  <point name="target_position" color="0 .5 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Aiming target for entities like light, misc_portal_camera and trigger_push (jump pads) in particular. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">the entity that requires an aiming direction points to this.</targetname>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
<real3 key="origin" name="World Origin">Aim point in world space.</real3>
-------- NOTES --------
To make a jump pad, place this entity at the highest point of the jump and target it with a trigger_push entity.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </point>

  <point name="target_print" color="0 .5 0" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
This will print a message on the center of the screen when triggered. By default, all the clients will see the message. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<string key="message" name="Message">text string to print on screen.</string>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">the activating trigger points to this.</targetname>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="SAMETEAM" name="Sameteam" bit="0">only players in activator's team will see the message.</flag>
<flag key="OTHERTEAM" name="Otherteam" bit="1">only players in other than activator's team will see the message.</flag>
<flag key="PRIVATE" name="Private" bit="2">only the player that activates the target will see the message.</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </point>

  <point name="target_speaker" color="0 .7 .7" box="-8 -8 -8 8 8 8">
Normal sounds play each time the target is used.  The reliable flag can be set for crucial voiceovers. Looped sounds are always atten 3 / vol 1, and the use function toggles it on/off. Multiple identical looping sounds will just increase volume without any speed cost. (updated: 12/08/2005)
-------- KEYS --------
<sound key="noise" name="Sound File">path/name of .wav file to play (eg. sound/world/growl1.wav - see Notes).</sound>
<real key="volume" name="Volume">Documented in older references but not read by the current game. Use the attenuation key to control how far the sound carries.</real>
<integer key="attenuation" name="Sound Attenuation">Sound attenuation: -1 = none (whole level), 1 = normal fighting sounds, 2 = idle sounds, 3 = ambient sounds.</integer>
<real key="wait" name="Delay">delay in seconds between each time the sound is played ("random" key must be set - see Notes).</real>
<real key="random" name="Delay Variance">random time variance in seconds added or subtracted from "wait" delay ("wait" key must be set - see Notes).</real>
<targetname key="targetname" name="Target Name">the activating button or trigger points to this.</targetname>
<boolean key="notfree" name="Hidden for Solo">Set to 1 to hide this entity in non-team-based gametypes (ffa, dm, duel, race, ...) and in team gametypes limited to one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notduel" name="Hidden for Duels">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with exactly one player per team.</boolean>
<boolean key="notteam" name="Hidden for Teamplay">Set to 1 to hide this entity in team-based gametypes with more than one player per team (e.g. CTF, TDM).</boolean>
<string key="gametype" name="Supported Game Types">Comma- or space-separated allow-list of gametype names in which this entity will spawn; if set, it will not spawn in any other gametype. Names are case-insensitive. See the supported gametype values note below.</string>
<string key="not_gametype" name="Excluded Game Types">Comma- or space-separated deny-list of gametype names in which this entity must not spawn. Uses the same values as the gametype key.</string>
-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
<flag key="LOOPED_ON" name="Looped On" bit="0">sound will loop and initially start on in level (will toggle on/off when triggered).</flag>
<flag key="LOOPED_OFF" name="Looped Off" bit="1">sound will loop and initially start off in level (will toggle on/off when triggered).</flag>
<flag key="RELIABLE" name="Reliable" bit="2"></flag>
<flag key="GLOBAL" name="Global" bit="3">Overrides attenuation setting. Sound will play full volume throughout the level as if it had attenuation -1</flag>
<flag key="ACTIVATOR" name="Activator" bit="4">sound will play only for the player that activated the target.</flag>
-------- NOTES --------
The path portion value of the "noise" key can be replaced by the implicit folder character "*" for triggered sounds that belong to a particular player model. For example, if you want to create a "bottomless pit" in which the player screams and dies when he falls into, you would place a trigger_multiple over the floor of the pit and target a target_speaker with it. Then, you would set the "noise" key to "*falling1.wav". The * character means the current player model's sound folder. So if your current player model is Visor, * = sound/player/visor, if your current player model is Sarge, * = sound/player/sarge, etc. This cool feature provides an excellent way to create "player-specific" triggered sounds in your levels.
Supported gametype values: Bomb and Defuse: bomb, Clan Arena: ca, Capture the Flag: ctf, Capture the Flag Tactics: ctftactics, Duel Arena: da, Deathmatch: dm, Tournament: duel, Free for All: ffa, Headhunt: headhunt, Race: race, Rekt: rekt, Team Deathmatch: tdm, Tutorial: tutorial.
  </point>

  <point name="props_skyportal" color=".6 .7 .7" box="-8 -8 0 8 8 16">
-------- KEYS --------
<real key="fov" name="Field of View">for the skybox default is whatever client's fov is set to</real>
<real key="scale" name="View Scale">is world/skyarea ratio if you want to keep a certain perspective when player moves around the world</real>
<boolean key="noents" name="Hide Sky Entities">makes the skyportal ignore entities within the sky area, making them invisible for the player</boolean>
  </point>


<!--
=============================================================================

 MAKEBSP ENTITIES

=============================================================================
-->

  <group name="func_trisoup" color="0 .5 .8">
Compiler-only entity that turns its brushes and patches into a single smooth triangle soup with unique lightmap UVs. Geometry stays in the BSP.
-------- KEYS --------
<real key="shadeangle" name="Smooth Angle">Smooth-normal blend threshold in degrees (default 46).</real>
<real key="subdivide" name="Subdivide">Patch flattening tolerance (default 6.0). Alias: subdivisions.</real>
<real key="smooth" name="Lightmap Smooth Radius">Lightmap smoothing radius (0 disables).</real>
<string key="smoothgroup" name="Smooth Group">Shared smoothing group name.</string>
<color key="vertexcolor" name="Vertex Color">Override the vertex color.</color>
<real key="vertexalpha" name="Vertex Alpha">Override opacity (0..1 or 0..255).</real>
<boolean key="upscale" name="Upscale Raytracing">Raytrace at 2x lightmap resolution.</boolean>
<real key="supersample" name="Supersample Radius">Supersampling trace radius (0 = off).</real>
<real key="samplesize" name="Lightmap Sample Size">Lightmap sample size override. Alias: lightmapsamplesize.</real>
<boolean key="enforcesamplesize" name="Enforce Sample Size">Subdivide to honour the sample size.</boolean>
<string key="decalgroup" name="Decal Group">Only decals with a matching decalgroup project here.</string>
<boolean key="nosolid" name="Render Only">Render without collision. Also nonsolid / collisiontype none.</boolean>
-------- NOTES --------
Chamfer width keys are currently inactive for trisoup geometry.
collisiontype none (also nonsolid) is accepted by the compiler for render-only geometry; it has no editor widget.
  </group>

  <group name="func_light" color="0 .5 .8">
Compiler-only entity whose brush faces emit point, spot or surface lights. The entity itself is consumed by the compiler, but its brushes are kept: they are moved into worldspawn and remain part of the BSP. Only visible faces generate light - faces using nodraw, skip, sky or similar non-drawn shaders are ignored.
-------- KEYS --------
<string key="type" name="Light Type">point, spot (default), or surface. Aliases: pointlight, spotlight, surfacelight.</string>
<real key="nudge" name="Face Offset">Offset from the brush face (default 1.0 spot / 0.01 point).</real>
<real key="light" name="Intensity">Emission intensity.</real>
<color key="_color" name="Light Color">Light color; derived from the surface lightimage if omitted.</color>
<real key="backsplash" name="Backsplash">Backsplash fraction (0..1).</real>
<real key="subdivide" name="Surface Subdivision">Surface-light subdivision fineness.</real>
<real key="radius" name="Spot Radius">Spot radius at the target (default 64).</real>
<real key="softness" name="Spot Softness">Spot edge softness (default 1).</real>
<target key="target" name="Target">Spotlight aim target.</target>
<direction key="dir" name="Direction">Spotlight aim direction.</direction>
<angles key="angles" name="Pitch Yaw Roll">Spotlight aim angles.</angles>
<real key="prestep" name="Singularity Offset">Offset from the face (default 16). Aliases: rampoffset, extradist.</real>
<string key="attenuation" name="Falloff Model">standard, soft, linear, unreal, smoothstep.</string>
<real key="cutoff" name="Cutoff">Auto-scaled cutoff anchor.</real>
<real key="energycutoff" name="Absolute Energy Cutoff">Absolute energy cull threshold.</real>
<real key="fadeout" name="Fade Out">Soft fade fraction.</real>
<boolean key="nodeluxe" name="No Deluxe">Exclude from deluxe direction maps.</boolean>
<boolean key="backsplash_nodeluxe" name="No Backsplash Deluxe">Exclude backsplash from deluxe maps.</boolean>
<real key="grid_ambientscale" name="Grid Ambient Scale">Grid ambient contribution multiplier (default 1).</real>
<real key="grid_directscale" name="Grid Direct Scale">Grid direct contribution multiplier (default 1).</real>
<real key="grid_maxambient" name="Grid Max Ambient">Ambient grid luma cap (0 = uncapped).</real>
<real key="grid_maxdirect" name="Grid Max Direct">Direct grid luma cap (0 = uncapped).</real>
<texture key="haloshader" name="Halo Shader">Light halo shader ("none" or "0" disables).</texture>
<real key="haloscale" name="Halo Scale">Halo size multiplier (default 1).</real>
-------- BRUSH SURFACE OVERRIDES --------
<real key="smooth" name="Lightmap Smooth Radius">Lightmap smoothing radius for this entity's surfaces (0 disables).</real>
<color key="vertexcolor" name="Vertex Color">Override the vertex color.</color>
<real key="vertexalpha" name="Vertex Alpha">Override opacity (0..1 or 0..255).</real>
<boolean key="upscale" name="Upscale Raytracing">Raytrace this entity's surfaces at 2x lightmap resolution.</boolean>
<real key="supersample" name="Supersample Radius">Supersampling trace radius (0 = off).</real>
<real key="samplesize" name="Lightmap Sample Size">Lightmap sample size override. Alias: lightmapsamplesize.</real>
<boolean key="enforcesamplesize" name="Enforce Sample Size">Subdivide brushes/patches to honour the sample size.</boolean>
<boolean key="castshadows" name="Cast Shadows">Cast shadows into the lightmap (default 1). Alias: cs.</boolean>
<string key="modelgroup" name="Model Group">Bind misc_model entities with the same modelgroup to this entity.</string>
<string key="decalgroup" name="Decal Group">Only decals with a matching decalgroup project onto these surfaces.</string>
<real key="chamfer_convexwidth" name="Convex Chamfer Width">Per-entity convex-edge chamfer width.</real>
<real key="chamfer_concavewidth" name="Concave Chamfer Width">Per-entity concave-edge chamfer width.</real>
<boolean key="nosolid" name="Render Only">Render the brushes without collision. Also nonsolid / collisiontype none.</boolean>
-------- NOTES --------
collisiontype none (also nonsolid) is accepted by the compiler for render-only brushes; it has no editor widget.
  </group>

  <group name="func_trim" color="0 .5 .8">
Compiler-only entity: its brush faces act as infinite cutting planes that slice misc_model meshes. The entity and its brushes are removed from the BSP.
-------- KEYS --------
<target key="target" name="Target">Only cut misc_model entities whose targetname matches. Leave blank to cut all models.</target>
-------- NOTES --------
Faces using nodraw / skip shaders are ignored as cutting planes.
  </group>

  <group name="func_terrain" color="0 .5 .8">
Compiler-only terrain generator. Child brushes become invisible collision geometry while the visible terrain is generated from the keys below.
-------- KEYS --------
<texture key="shader" name="Terrain MetaShader">Metashader used to assign terrain textures.</texture>
<texture key="alphamap" name="Terrain Blending Map">Art file guiding texture blending.</texture>
<integer key="layers" name="Terrain Layers">Number of unique root shaders used by the terrain.</integer>
  </group>

  <point name="misc_decal" color=".22 .522 1" box="-4 -4 -4 4 4 4">
Point decal projector that generates a quad and projects a shader onto nearby geometry.
-------- KEYS --------
<texture key="shader" name="Decal Shader">Shader to project (default textures/common/nodraw).</texture>
<real key="width" name="Width">Quad width (default shader image size / 4 or 64).</real>
<real key="height" name="Height">Quad height (default shader image size / 4 or 64).</real>
<real key="scale" name="Scale">Proportional size multiplier (default 1).</real>
<real key="distance" name="Projection Depth">Projection depth (default 64). Alias: depth.</real>
<angles key="angles" name="Pitch Yaw Roll">Projection direction; pitch 90 points straight down.</angles>
<angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle">Yaw-only projection direction when angles is unset.</angle>
<target key="target" name="Target">Aim target entity for the projection.</target>
<real key="rotate" name="Rotation">Rotate the quad clockwise around the projection axis.</real>
<string key="decalgroup" name="Decal Group">Only project onto receivers with a matching decalgroup.</string>
<color key="vertexcolor" name="Vertex Color">Decal vertex color override. Alias: _color.</color>
<real key="vertexalpha" name="Vertex Alpha">Decal opacity override.</real>
-------- NOTES --------
The default projection direction is +X.
  </point>

  <point name="misc_text_decal" color="0 .5 .8" box="-4 -4 -4 4 4 4">
Point entity that generates text geometry from a TrueType font atlas.
-------- KEYS --------
<string key="text" name="Text">Text to render.</string>
<texture key="font" name="Font Atlas">Font atlas descriptor (fallback keys: shader, texture).</texture>
<real key="height" name="Glyph Height">Glyph height in world units (default 32). Alias: size.</real>
<string key="align" name="Horizontal Align">left (default), center/middle, right.</string>
<string key="valign" name="Vertical Align">baseline (default), top, center/middle, bottom.</string>
<real key="tracking" name="Tracking">Inter-character spacing (default 0).</real>
<real key="distance" name="Projection Depth">Projection depth (default 64). Alias: depth.</real>
<angles key="angles" name="Pitch Yaw Roll">Projection direction.</angles>
<angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle">Yaw-only projection direction when angles is unset.</angle>
<target key="target" name="Target">Aim target entity for the projection.</target>
<real key="rotate" name="Rotation">Rotate the text clockwise around the projection axis.</real>
<string key="decalgroup" name="Decal Group">Only project onto receivers with a matching decalgroup.</string>
<color key="vertexcolor" name="Vertex Color">Vertex color override. Alias: _color.</color>
<real key="vertexalpha" name="Vertex Alpha">Opacity override.</real>
  </point>


</classes>
